  '<h3 class="gd-h3">Who this guide is for</h3><p class="gd-p">Investors with an Investment Agreement with CarmaCars. Your portal shows each investment, what it has earned and paid, your monthly statements, and lets you send notices to us.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">What you need</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The invitation email from CarmaCars (investor accounts are by invitation only)</li><li>Access to that inbox: the link works for 24 hours, once</li><li>An authenticator app, if you choose two-step sign-in (recommended)</li></ul><section class="gd-task" id="start-here-your-first-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your first sign-in</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the invitation email and press its link within 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a password of 8 characters or more and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the new password</b>. You land on Home.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Next time, sign in at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/sign-in</span>, or use Investor sign in at the bottom of any page of carmacars.ca.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forgot your password? Press <b class="gd-ui">Forgot your password?</b> on the sign-in page.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/645"><img src="/guides/img/public-09-sign-in-phone-1f766061.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="645"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95.4%;top:78.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Link expired? The page it opens has <b class="gd-ui">Send me a new link</b>.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'your-investments', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'Investments shows each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.

## Read an investment

1. The tabs: **Investments**, **Live sheets**, **Statements**, **Documents to sign**, **Investor deck** (while CarmaCars shares it) and **Profile and notices**. **Guide** and **Sign out** are at the top.
2. Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.
3. Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under "Principal, dates and amounts to date".
4. Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.
5. Latest statement, with **Open**.

![](/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg "phone; size: 390 1605; pins: 1 25.6 15.3, 2 38.5 34.9, 3 51.3 72.6, 5 51.3 95.0")

> Tip: This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.

## Live sheets

**Live sheets** is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.

1. **My investment**: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch **Paid monthly** or **Reinvested** to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Profile and notices).
2. **Calculator**: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.
3. **How it works**: the terms in plain words, step by step, with examples.
4. **Fund a car**: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.
5. **Download as Excel** gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. **Download as PDF** gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.

> Tip: The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.

## Sign your investment agreement

When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents to sign.

1. Press **Documents to sign** in the menu. The top shows what is signed ("0 of 1 signed").
2. Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.
3. Press **Read the PDF** and read it, with its schedules.
4. Say whether you got independent legal advice.
5. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
6. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.

Once you sign, the agreement shows "Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars" under Signed. CarmaCars''s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.

> Tip: Signed on paper instead? Once we record it, it shows under Signed with the scan.
', 'Your investments', 'Each investment, its returns and the latest statement.',
  'Home shows what needs you first (a document to sign, a notice, a return on hold), then each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.

## Read an investment

1. The menu: **Home**, **Live sheets**, **Documents** (with the tabs **Statements**, **Documents to sign** and **Your files**), **Investor deck** (while CarmaCars shares it) and **Account**. **Guide** and **Sign out** are at the top.
2. Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.
3. Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under "Principal, dates and amounts to date".
4. Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.
5. Latest statement, with **Open**.

![](/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg "phone; size: 390 1605; pins: 1 25.6 15.3, 2 38.5 34.9, 3 51.3 72.6, 5 51.3 95.0")

> Tip: This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.

## Live sheets

**Live sheets** is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.

1. **My investment**: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch **Paid monthly** or **Reinvested** to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Account).
2. **Calculator**: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.
3. **How it works**: the terms in plain words, step by step, with examples.
4. **Fund a car**: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.
5. **Download as Excel** gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. **Download as PDF** gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.

> Tip: The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.

## Sign your investment agreement

When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents, Documents to sign, and first on Home.

1. Press **Read and sign** on Home, or open **Documents** > **Documents to sign**. The top shows what is signed ("0 of 1 signed").
2. Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.
3. Press **Read the PDF** and read it, with its schedules.
4. Say whether you got independent legal advice.
5. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
6. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.

Once you sign, the agreement shows "Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars" under Signed. CarmaCars''s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.

> Tip: Signed on paper instead? Once we record it, it shows under Signed with the scan.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Home shows what needs you first (a document to sign, a notice, a return on hold), then each of your investments: what you put in, what it earns, and when it pays.</p><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-read-an-investment" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read an investment</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: <b class="gd-ui">Home</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Live sheets</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> (with the tabs <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Documents to sign</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Your files</b>), <b class="gd-ui">Investor deck</b> (while CarmaCars shares it) and <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Guide</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Sign out</b> are at the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Your agreement number and name, your Invested Amount, the Returns paid to date (or reinvested) and the next payment, with a chart of your account month by month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each investment: its Invested Amount, how far the lockup period has run, the Yearly Percentage, how Returns are handled (Paid monthly or Reinvested) and the Next Payment Date. Principal, what was reinvested and redeemed to date, the Investment Date and the Lockup End Date are under &quot;Principal, dates and amounts to date&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Payment schedule: the last Returns on your statements and the next ones. An amount that is not on a statement yet is marked Estimated.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Latest statement, with <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/1605"><img src="/guides/img/investor-01-investments-phone-16342025.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="1605"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.6%;top:15.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.5%;top:34.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.3%;top:72.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.3%;top:95%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>This area shows your records under your Investment Agreement. It is not an offer or a solicitation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-live-sheets" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Live sheets</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Live sheets</b> is the CarmaCars investment workbook on the website, filled in from your own records. It updates itself: when a payment to you is recorded, it shows as Paid on your next visit.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">My investment</b>: your Invested Amount, start date, Yearly Percentage, lockup end, the payouts made so far and the next payout with its date. Below is your schedule: your statements as recorded (Paid, To be paid, On hold, Reinvested), then the months ahead (Projected). Switch <b class="gd-ui">Paid monthly</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Reinvested</b> to compare the months ahead; it does not change your choice (that is a request under Account).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Calculator</b>: type an amount (at least the minimum), a start date and a yearly percentage, and choose Paid monthly or Reinvested. You see the monthly payout, when the lockup ends, the first payment, what is paid by months 24 and 36, and the 36-month schedule. It starts from your own numbers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How it works</b>: the terms in plain words, step by step, with examples.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fund a car</b>: for buying a car and placing it in the owner program. Type the price, the daily rate, the days you expect it rented and the terms of your owner agreement. You see your monthly payout, the yearly figures, the return on the car and the payout schedule. Add up to three cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b> gives you the same sheets as a spreadsheet with working formulas, with your numbers filled in. <b class="gd-ui">Download as PDF</b> gives your investment, your schedule and how it works on a few pages.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The sheets show only your own records and the investment terms. The months ahead are estimates; your monthly statement is the record.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="your-investments-sign-your-investment-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign your investment agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">When CarmaCars sends your agreement, it is under Documents, Documents to sign, and first on Home.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b> on Home, or open <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Documents to sign</b>. The top shows what is signed (&quot;0 of 1 signed&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values: your name and address, the Invested Amount, the Yearly Percentage and the dates. The agreement is filled in from your record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it, with its schedules.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Say whether you got independent legal advice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the risk acknowledgment (Schedule C), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is on the same page.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Once you sign, the agreement shows &quot;Awaiting countersignature by CarmaCars&quot; under Signed. CarmaCars&#39;s signing officer countersigns it; the agreement binds CarmaCars once it is countersigned and your funds have cleared. You get the countersigned copy on the same page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Signed on paper instead? Once we record it, it shows under Signed with the scan.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'how-your-returns-work', 'chapter', 'your-investments', 'Your return is worked out month by month on the Invested Amount, at the Yearly Percentage in your agreement. Here is the cycle and the words your statements use.

## The monthly cycle

:::flow
Return Month | Your Invested Amount earns for each day of the month
Statement | The return is worked out after the month ends
The 15th | Paid to your bank account, or reinvested
Email | Your statement, with its PDF attached
:::

- No return is earned for the lockup period. Your first Return Month starts on your Lockup End Date.
- Paid monthly: the return is paid by bank transfer on the 15th of the month after the Return Month (the Next Payment Date).
- Reinvested: the return is added to your Invested Amount, so it earns from then on.
- Each statement shows the Invested Amount at the start and the end of the month, so you can follow it over time.

## The words on your statements

| Term | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Invested Amount | What is earning a return: your principal, plus returns reinvested, less amounts redeemed. |
| Principal | What you invested. |
| Yearly Percentage | The yearly rate in your agreement. |
| Investment Date | The day your funds cleared. |
| Lockup End Date | Six months after the Investment Date. No return is earned before it. |
| Return Month | The calendar month a return is earned in. |
| Days earning | How many days of the month the amount earned, for example 31 of 31. |
| Next Payment Date | When the next return is paid: the 15th of the month after the Return Month. |

## Notices from CarmaCars

Two notices can appear on Investments, under Needs your attention, above your investments:

| Notice | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Return on hold: | A return is held, with the reason, for example tax information we still need. Send what it asks for and we release it. |
| Redemption notice: | CarmaCars will repay an amount, with the Redemption Date. |

## Emails you get from us

- Your statement is ready, with the PDF attached, each month.
- Your return was paid, with the amount and date (not sent when it is reinvested).
- We received your notice: an election change, a bank account change or a contact change.

> Tip: Our investor emails are servicing notices about your existing investment. They are not an offer or a solicitation. CarmaCars gives no tax advice.

## Texts or email

On **Profile and notices**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both**. Texts need a phone you verified with a code and link to the page. Statements are always emailed. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.
', 'How your returns work', 'The monthly cycle, the terms on your statements, notices and holds.',
